[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2542398494","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100378#issuecomment-2542398494","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100378","id":2542398494,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Xiewe","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-13T21:18:27Z","updated_at":"2024-12-13T21:18:32Z","body":"> Accordingly we can modulo this with the lifetime and save a ton of processing time.\r\n\r\nShouldn't we use `min(lifetime, preprocess_time)` instead? If you have particles with a lifetime of 1 second and preprocess set to 1.5 seconds, I'd expect the full lifetime to be preprocessed instead of preprocessing only 0.5 seconds.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2542398494/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2542543871","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100378#issuecomment-2542543871","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100378","id":2542543871,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XjCP_","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-13T23:28:19Z","updated_at":"2024-12-13T23:28:19Z","body":"> > Accordingly we can modulo this with the lifetime and save a ton of processing time.\r\n> \r\n> Shouldn't we use `min(lifetime, preprocess_time)` instead? If you have particles with a lifetime of 1 second and preprocess set to 1.5 seconds, I'd expect the full lifetime to be preprocessed instead of preprocessing only 0.5 seconds.\r\n\r\nNo, the purpose of preprocess is to start your shader mid way through the lifetime of the particles. Using min would totally defeat the purpose of using preprocess altogether. It would guarantee that the particles behaviour is the same as if preprocess wasn't used at all.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2542543871/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2543091910","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100378#issuecomment-2543091910","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100378","id":2543091910,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XlIDG","user":{"login":"JoNax97","id":10124534,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTI0NTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10124534?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97","html_url":"https://github.com/JoNax97","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-14T12:43:18Z","updated_at":"2024-12-14T12:43:18Z","body":"Would it make sense to expose this as a bounded 0-1 range that repents a % of the particle lifetime instead of absolute time in seconds? ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2543091910/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2543309800","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100378#issuecomment-2543309800","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100378","id":2543309800,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Xl9Po","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-14T18:50:03Z","updated_at":"2024-12-14T18:50:03Z","body":"> Using min would totally defeat the purpose of using preprocess altogether.\r\n\r\nBut the min would ensure only that preprocess doesn't exceed lifetime.\r\n\r\nWe can also set a dynamic property range based on lifetime.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2543309800/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2547369113","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100378#issuecomment-2547369113","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100378","id":2547369113,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6X1cSZ","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-17T02:29:32Z","updated_at":"2024-12-17T02:29:32Z","body":"> Would it make sense to expose this as a bounded 0-1 range that repents a % of the particle lifetime instead of absolute time in seconds?\r\n\r\nPerhaps. My understanding of preprocess is that it is used to get the particle simulation to a certain point before it becomes visible, in which case I think absolute time or absolute frames are necessary for artists to actually control the effect. Making it a % of lifetime means that it would need to manually be adjusted each time that lifetime is adjusted. \r\n\r\n> > Using min would totally defeat the purpose of using preprocess altogether.\r\n> \r\n> But the min would ensure only that preprocess doesn't exceed lifetime.\r\n\r\nI should clarify, there are two conditions with a min:\r\n1. Preprocess is less than lifetime: Min does nothing\r\n2. Preprocess is greater than lifetime: preprocess does nothing\r\n\r\n> We can also set a dynamic property range based on lifetime.\r\n\r\nI think this would be very nice too, but it won't help people that use `RenderingServer.particles_set_pre_process_time()` directly. However, it would probably be much nicer for the editor. How do you set a dynamic property range?\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2547369113/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2549379606","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100378#issuecomment-2549379606","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100378","id":2549379606,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6X9HIW","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-17T19:06:33Z","updated_at":"2024-12-17T19:07:13Z","body":"> Preprocess is greater than lifetime: preprocess does nothing\r\n\r\nOnly if explosiveness is 1, so all particles disappear with lifetime. Otherwise you have particles spawned in-between lifetimes and preprocessing full lifetime has visible effect.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2549379606/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2549784585","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100378#issuecomment-2549784585","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100378","id":2549784585,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6X-qAJ","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-17T22:30:01Z","updated_at":"2024-12-17T22:30:01Z","body":"> > Preprocess is greater than lifetime: preprocess does nothing\r\n> \r\n> Only if explosiveness is 1, so all particles disappear with lifetime. Otherwise you have particles spawned in-between lifetimes and preprocessing full lifetime has visible effect.\r\n\r\nOh, right. I was confusing a cycle with lifetime. After a cycle all the particles will be back to the same position they would have been in if you only cycled once. Cycling 1.5 times is the same as cycling 0.5 times for example. \r\n\r\nIndeed, with explosiveness at 0 (and one shot disabled) then a cycle is `2 * lifetime` and preprocessing up to `2 * lifetime` will do something.\r\n\r\nAt any rate, this PR doesn't even change that, so no reason to hold this PR back...","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2549784585/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2549906423","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100378#issuecomment-2549906423","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100378","id":2549906423,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6X_Hv3","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-17T23:40:55Z","updated_at":"2024-12-17T23:40:55Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2549906423/